---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
import SeoNav from '../../components/SeoNav.astro';
---

<!--
	`seo={false}` emits nothing but a <title>, and `htmlLang={false}` drops the
	lang attribute. This is the state a page is in before anyone has thought
	about how it gets shared.
-->
<Layout
	title="Bare head"
	lede="A title and nothing else, which is what most pages start as."
	seo={false}
	htmlLang={false}
>
	<SeoNav />

	<Callout title="What to try" tone="accent">
		Open the share preview. Every card falls back to the document title and
		renders without an image, and each one is marked with what it had to do
		without. This is what the link looks like when somebody pastes it.
	</Callout>

	<section class="panel" aria-label="What this page does not declare">
		<h2>What is missing</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>No <code>meta description</code>, so Google writes its own snippet from the page text.</li>
			<li>No <code>og:title</code> or <code>og:description</code>, so cards fall back to the document title and render with an empty body.</li>
			<li>No <code>og:image</code>, so every card is a text-only link.</li>
			<li>No <code>twitter:card</code>, so X shows the small square rather than the banner.</li>
			<li>No <code>og:url</code> or canonical link, so the same page shared with different query strings counts as different links.</li>
			<li>No <code>lang</code> on <code>&lt;html&gt;</code>, so search engines and screen readers both guess.</li>
			<li>No icon, so Google shows a generic globe and Slack loses the site mark.</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<Callout title="The fallbacks are the point">
		Nothing here is an accident of the fixture. Each card shows the tag chain
		its network falls back through when the tag it wants is absent — which is
		why the same bare page still looks different on Google, X and WhatsApp.
	</Callout>
</Layout>

<style>
	.panel {
		border: 1px dashed #78551c;
		border-radius: 8px;
		padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
	}

	h2 {
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
	}

	ul {
		color: #aeb6c5;
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.35rem;
		margin: 0;
		padding-left: 1.1rem;
	}

	code {
		color: #fcd34d;
		font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace;
	}
</style>
